Z||000000||Philphine||08-21-2000||10:21 AM||||<BR>pretty sure i need them on my '87 4 cyl. how hard to do? can i kind of "unweigh" the engine in the cradle and change them? do i need to lift car and then lift engine further? haven't looked in my hanes yet so i may be asking an obvious question, but i would appreciate any hints and advice. thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||2birds||08-21-2000||11:10 AM||||I changed my trnsaxle mounts while the cradle was out.  I think it would be really difficult, due to "room to work" with the engine and cradle still in the car.  I did the front engine mount in place, though, using a jack and a board under the pan.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-21-2000||03:42 PM||||The 4 cyl mount is under the oil pan. you'll see how it comes out as soon as you look at it. Yes, you need to lift the motor to unload it. If you put a jack under the oil pan put a big block of wood between the pan and jack to spread the load or you'll crush the pan.<P>The tranny depends on which tranny. the auto will be a single mount pretty much like the motor. the manual will have 2 mounts.<P>If you have an automatic read over the article about the torque struts in the cave. before messing with mounts. (Link at bottom of page.)<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||08-22-2000||07:57 AM||||Philphine:  I just did my '87's mounts and TRS back in May/June (with the help of fiero56!).  You don't have to lift the car first but it does give you more room to work.<P>As Ogre said, loosen the mounts then lift the engine/transaxle with a floor jack and a thick (and wide!) piece of wood.  Wide wood allows the weight to be better distributed (not as important when you lift the transaxle side but DEFINITELY important when you lift the engine side under the oil pan!).<P>I don't know how the automatics are (mine's a 5-speed) but the forward tranny mount on the manuals is wrapped by a heat shield to protect it from the exhaust pipe that runs right beside it.  The replacement mount I bought from The Fiero Store didn't come with the shield so I had to remove the shield from the old one and install it on the new one.  Just make sure you keep this in mind.<P>Hope this helps.  If you have any questions, please feel free to contact me.||||reg||1
